q_engine.exe is essentially a clipboard daemon/utility designed with a minimalist dumb saver architecture. Simply put, it acts as an intelligent clipboard manager that processes the following types of clipboard content:
1. Plain text: Reads and records text content from the system clipboard
2. Files/Folders: Copies files/folders from the clipboard to a designated directory (supports batch and parallel copying)
3. Images: Extracts screenshots in CF_DIB/CF_DIBV5 format from the clipboard and saves them as PNG files
4. HTML content: Reads HTML-formatted content from the clipboard (with optional Base64 encoding)
In addition to the core clipboard processing, it also provides a full set of auxiliary features:
1. Folder size & file type statistics (with cancelable time-consuming scanning)
2. File icon extraction and conversion to Base64 encoding
3. Reading/setting of clipboard file lists
4. System-level file pasting (supports background copying of large files and special path processing)
5. Communication with external programs (e.g., Node.js/VS Code) via a specific JSON protocol
We hereby request a re-review of the qqq extension. Please point out any existing issues, and we will attach great importance to and follow up on them promptly.
